    "done_when": "tests/renderer_wall_scan.py reports each unguarded call by its repository-relative path and line (not the basename), so docs/figures/centroid-constrained-oracle-solve/repaired-remeasure/measure.py and repaired-remeasure-receipt/measure.py are distinct records, and it treats a draw_flux_contours call as wall-guarded when the wall is passed positionally as well as by keyword (nova/media/poloidal.py declares wall as a positional parameter). The exemption list documents every entry it holds with its reason. tests/test_renderer_wall_scan.py keeps the controls (flags plasma_cell_fixed_point_attribution.py:424 and sol_ledger_current_census.py:415, passes closed-forms/render.py:52 and contour_tree_explanatory_figure.py:359, ignores the post-filtered probe at plasma_cell_trip_panels.py:406) and adds a positional-wall control, but asserts no total count of unguarded sites, so a repair that removes sites cannot turn it red; the per-site reconciliation against the inventory moves to a committed report script under docs/figures/figure-and-solver-audit/fsa-renderer-wall-scanner-guard-form/ that prints the current list with relative paths and exits zero. The command-line entry accepts a list of files and exits nonzero when any of them holds an unguarded call, which is the gate each repair batch will run on its own files. Gate: JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_renderer_wall_scan.py passes with zero added failures against the base, with a recorded baseline arm.",
